- Redis cross-pod path: router wires eventHub.SubscribeRedis at internal\api\router.go:236; SubscribeRedis subscribes at internal\api\sse_handler.go:92 and forwards preformatted payloads to local clients at internal\api\sse_handler.go:95-110.
- Telemetry publisher path: internal\api\telemetry_handler.go:1244-1263 publishes through Redis when h.redisCache exists. internal\api\telemetry_handler.go:1258 calls PublishSignals.
- Fallback behavior: internal\api\telemetry_handler.go:1249-1252 falls back to local broadcast on marshal failure; internal\api\telemetry_handler.go:1258-1260 falls back to local broadcast on Redis publish failure; internal\api\telemetry_handler.go:1266-1267 uses local broadcast when Redis is absent.
- Contract risk: when Redis is configured, the local originating pod receives the event through its own SubscribeRedis subscription rather than direct Broadcast on the success path. Pub/Sub is not durable replay; disconnected clients recover only via later reads.

